  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2e965f9168c2046c28c59aa4b83cc1ec, type: 3}
  m_Name: FlightCatch
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GravityBox.Gameplay::GravityBox.Gameplay.LevelDefinition
  Id: steel-lab-flightcatch
  DisplayIndex: 21
  DisplayName: Catch me
  Shape: 20
  TeachingHint: Build speed on the ramp. Rotate the receiving trough under the flying
    ball.
  Environment: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 82e0ce24addfe4fc89b8bbd0db998aea, type: 2}
  Prefab: {fileID: 8979698347520386273, guid: b739b1c5300b3435792321e58209dc9f, type: 3}
  RotationMode: 1
  InitialLocalVelocity: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  ParSeconds: 0
  Tutorial: 0
  DesignerSolution: Gravity and rolling contact accelerate the steel ball down the
    takeoff ramp. During the unsupported flight the ball keeps its world-space trajectory
    while the player reorients the enclosure and receiving trough. Land in the receiving
    route and reach the real circular exit. A missed catch returns through the recovery
    route; no launch impulse or airborne attraction is added. Shared exit assist
    pulls the ball through an unobstructed opening within 40 mm. This is deliberate
    gameplay assistance; the entire sphere must still physically clear the bore before
    completion.
